		<item>
		<title>Round the World Trip 🌍 🤩 from Dublin for €919: Canada ✈ The USA ✈ Singapore ✈ Malaysia ✈ Vietnam</title>
		<link>https://www.fly4free.com/flight-deals/europe/round-the-world-trip-from-dublin/</link>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Maria Shvab]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Wed, 04 Nov 2026 17:00:56 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[Europe]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[We recommend]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Around the world flight deals]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[around the world trip]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[asia deal]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[cheap flights from Dublin]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Dublin]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[tropical islands]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.fly4free.com/?p=779070</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[This is a proper round-the-world adventure, moving steadily west from Europe to Canada, crossing the Pacific into Southeast Asia, then continuing through Malaysia and Vietnam before returning to Dublin. And the variety is fantastic: Canadian mountains and waterfronts, an iconic rail journey to Seattle, futuristic Singapore, food-packed Kuala Lumpur and ten days to explore northern Vietnam — with planes, train and bus all forming part of the experience.]]></description>
		
		
		
			</item>
		<item>
		<title>10 Best Places to Spend Christmas as a Solo Traveller</title>
		<link>https://www.fly4free.com/news/christmas-with-strangers-10-places-around-the-world-for-solo-travellers/</link>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Dmytro]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Wed, 04 Nov 2026 16:54:59 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Christmas 2026]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Christmas celebration]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Christmas party]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[solo travel]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.fly4free.com/?p=778721</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[No one to spend Christmas with this year? In New York, you can head to a singles party, in Berlin, attend a free Christmas Eve gala, or in Paris, share a festive meal with strangers, exchange gifts and dance until 2am. For those looking for something quieter, there’s the option of spending a few days at a Swiss monastery or enjoying a traditional Christmas dinner in Finland. We’ve found 10 places where you can organise your own Christmas getaway in 2026 without having to spend the festive season alone.]]></description>
		
		
		
			</item>
